WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.434
-Welcome back to the program.
Thanks for being here.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.467
-Welcome back to you. How glad
are we that Jimmy is back?

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.968
-I am so happy.
-And the Roots are back!

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.667
-I am so happy.
I missed it so much.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:12.067
-This building's not the same
without you. It's lonely.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.767
-Is it?
-I come in here at 4:00 a.m.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.200
I come up here. I sleep
in your office, obviously.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.300
I play Quest's drums.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.467
-Yeah. We weren't allowed
in the building.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:20.934
I haven't been here
in five months.

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:22.567
-I know.
We're so glad you're back, man.

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.267
-I'm so happy to be back.
Thank you, buddy.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:28.400
I'm so thankful. I missed this.
This is so good for my ego.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.434
Yeah, I really needed this.
How's the fam?

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.133
How are the kids?
How's everybody?

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:34.701
-Good. Good.
I've got two teenagers now.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.868
It's coming for you, too.
Not yet, but it's coming.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.167
I've got a 16-year-old
and a 14-year-old.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.868
-I think you'd be good at this.

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:42.767
-We got great kids.
That's where you start.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:45.200
But also you start --
You start to feel your age.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.801
I'm pushing 50.
I don't know about you.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.267
-Me too. Me too.
-I'm on the cusp of it.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:52.334
-And we took our kids to
Gov Ball a couple of months ago,

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.567
which is this big music festival
in New York

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:57.501
where all, like, the hottest,
coolest bands play.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:58.968
-Oh, yeah.
-And we took 20

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.400
16-year-olds to see Gov Ball

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.834
and we put them on a bus, and
we were in an escort vehicle.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.467
We were not allowed on the bus.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.400
And we went with them to Queens
to this music concert,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.767
and we thought
we were pretty cool.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.100
-That's cool parents.
-But we went to the --

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.267
There's a tent they set up
for chaperones, basically.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:16.734
So we're lying in the tent.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:19.100
They have beds put out because
they know who you are,

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.968
and you kind of lie there
and play Wordle

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:24.901
and you listen to some bands...

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.734
while my daughter
and her friends are over

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:30.601
listening to Lil Uzi Vert
and Metro Boomin

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:33.701
and Ice Spice and Joey Badass

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.033
and all these bands
that they love.

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:36.434
-And you're playing Wordle
in a tent.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.567
-We're playing Wordle in a tent.
-Yeah. Okay. Yeah.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.434
-And so at one point,
we go over and we say,

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:43.200
"Let's be cool and hang out
with the kids," right?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.467
And so we're listening.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:47.100
And Joey Badass
says something like,

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.000
"Hey, to all the ladies..."

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.868
You know, it's really, like,
flattering to women.

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:54.734
And my wife goes, "You know
what? Thank you, Johnny Badass."

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.467
-Close. Close.
-And I said, "It's Joey.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:00.501
Let's get you back in the tent."

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.801
-[ Laughs ] Johnny Badass.
-Let's get you back in the tent.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:05.000
We'll have a mojito in the tent.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.667
-Yeah, we'll play
some more Wordle. Yeah.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.100
You know any five-letter words?
-Yeah.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.934
-I was gonna ask you
about some news headlines

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.167
and see what your take is
on everything.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:18.267
Nothing too crazy, but how about
what everyone's talking about?

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.601
Travis and Tay-Tay.

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:21.667
-You joke, but it is what
everyone's talking about.

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.601
I cover the news every day

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.133
and what's going on
with Donald Trump

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.634
and Kevin McCarthy and Congress
and all that.

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.834
And yet when on my phone
it pops up, I'm like,

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:33.834
"Babe! Travis Kelce's
jersey sales are up 400%!"

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:35.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.501
-It is every other headline.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.334
-She's like,
"That's not something."

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:40.634
But I don't know
exactly what's going on.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:42.667
I do have a little bit
of a theory.

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.901
I hope it's not controversial.
I'm happy for both of them.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:46.400
They seem like great people.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.901
-Is there any chance
that this is all

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.467
one big Capital One commercial?

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.767
In other words, are we gonna
go through weeks of this

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.634
and at the end they turn
to the camera and say,

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.300
"What's in your wallet?"
-Yeah, okay.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.367
No, no, I don't think --
I think this is real.

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.534
-Do you think it's real?
-I think it's as real as can be.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:03.634
-I hope it is. I think it is.

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:05.334
-And I think
they're both cool people.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.734
-Very cool.
-I think -- I would love --

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:09.567
It's almost like
when you see two people

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.267
that you go like,
"They should date."

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:12.834
Like,
"I want to be at that party.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:15.267
I want to be at this party."
-Yeah. No. I'm totally on board.

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.801
I just want to put it
in the universe,

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:19.133
if it happens, that I was right.

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:20.901
-It's a Capital One ad.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:22.267
-Let's talk about Trump.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:25.434
This is day three of
the Trump civil fraud trial.

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.701
I was gonna ask you, were you
surprised that he showed up?

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.367
Because he didn't
have to show up, right?

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:30.834
-You're right.
It's a civil trial.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.801
He doesn't have to be there
as a defendant.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.801
-Why is he there?
-So he shows up, in part,

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.200
I think,
to sit in that courtroom,

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.701
get the photograph
kind of glaring at the witnesses

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:41.567
and the judge and
and the district attorney

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.234
and everybody,
at the attorney general.

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:44.801
And then really
what he's there for

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.334
is the moment
where he walks out --

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:47.801
And he did it again today.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.367
He walks out of those doors
and he makes a speech

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.901
and he says this is a disgrace

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:53.601
and it's a witch hunt
and all of the other things.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:56.901
So like a lot of things
in his life, it's performative,

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:58.701
and he wants
to reinforce the idea

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:01.133
that this is
somehow a witch hunt.

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:04.234
But it does get to everything
he has built,

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.968
which is, "I'm a businessman.
I'm a successful guy.

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.667
I'm 'The Apprentice.'

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.701
And this is why I was elected.
This is why you know me."

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:13.367
And this civil trial
really gets at that,

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:14.801
which says --I don't know.

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:18.067
There was perhaps some fraud
involved in that whole image.

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:20.067
-Wow. Interesting.
That's an interesting take.

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:23.334
So. Yeah. Okay. Alright.
I see. I like that.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:25.467
-It's also a Capital One
commercial.

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:28.567
-You think he's doing a Capital
One commercial, as well?

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:29.968
-I do.
-How about this?

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:31.901
Yesterday,
the House voted to remove

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:34.100
Kevin McCarthy
as Speaker of the House.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.567
What happens now? Who takes
over? And what does it all mean?

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:39.000
-It's absolutely wild.
Kevin McCarthy desperately

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.968
wanted this job
for his entire career.

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:44.567
He had it for 269 days --
about 9 months.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:46.834
But to get the job,
he agreed to a rule

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.501
that said one member of Congress

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:51.667
can raise a motion
to get rid of him.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:53.667
And so the minute they didn't
like something he did,

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.467
they did it,
they took him up on it.

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:57.934
So it was a job he wanted
that he held for nine months.

00:04:57.934 --> 00:04:59.734
And it's not clear to me
who gets the job after --

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.300
There are names out there --

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.133
Steve Scalise and Jim Jordan
and some other people.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:05.767
But it's --
-Trump's name came up.

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:08.167
-Trump's name came up.
Yeah. Some people said,

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.467
"What if we just made Donald
Trump the Speaker of the House?"

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.634
-Speaker of the House?
-That's not gonna happen.

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:14.501
Don't worry.
That's not going to happen.

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:15.968
-I'm not gonna happen.
-No.

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:19.033
-And like everything else, this
is a Capital One commercial.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:21.300
What's happening now.
Is that too much?

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.567
-No, no. It's perfect.

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.434
I want to say,
I think you're coming up on

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:27.834
or just did your 300th episode
of "Sunday Today."

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.167
-Yeah, we just had our --

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:30.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:32.267
-I was one of the first.
-You were early.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.501
-I was in there early, right?

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:35.734
I was one of the first on

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:36.901
"Sunday Today
with Willie Geist."

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.901
-Jimmy was there very early
with, I think,

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:40.367
your first children's book.
-Yeah.

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:41.968
-Jimmy Fallon
was a guest on our show.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:43.534
-I loved doing you show.
-And also your ice cream.

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:44.901
Yeah, it was your
Ben &amp; Jerry's ice cream.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:47.601
-That's right. We had fun.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.934
-I know everyone asks
who your favorite guest is,

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:51.300
and you don't have to say.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.901
We all know, but...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:56.100
But who is your favorite type
of guest?

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.400
Is it a politician?
Is it a comedian?

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.868
-I love -- Yes.
Comedians are great.

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:03.968
I love a musician.
I love a musician. I do.

00:06:03.968 --> 00:06:06.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Unbelievable.

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:11.133
-What I love is hearing
how songs are built.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:12.968
I interviewed Jack Antonoff
yesterday.

00:06:12.968 --> 00:06:15.501
Actually, I saw Quest there
after I did that yesterday.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.501
I interviewed Jack Antonoff
talking about --

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:21.200
"So you and Taylor Swift
get in a room. Now what?

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.167
Like, how do you make
'1989' and 'Reputation'

00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:26.300
and 'Midnights'
and all that stuff?"

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.400
-Well, you're back with
a new episode of "Sunday Today"

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.968
this weekend.
Who do you have on this Sunday?

00:06:29.968 --> 00:06:31.968
-We got Darius Rucker.
The great Darius Rucker.

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:33.667
-Ooh. He's got a new record
coming out.

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:35.934
-He's got a new album
coming out.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:39.000
As, you know,
one of the all-time great guys.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.601
-He really is, man. He's solid.
-And what a ride, right?

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:44.300
Like, the Hootie &amp; the Blowfish
album

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.434
was the eighth-biggest-selling
album

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:48.834
in the history of bands,
in the history of music --

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:50.567
like, with the Eagles
and the Beatles

00:06:50.567 --> 00:06:52.634
and the Stones and Led Zeppelin
and all that.

00:06:52.634 --> 00:06:54.300
-They were a bar band, right?
North Carolina?

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.834
-Exactly.
College band in South Carolina.

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:56.934
-South Carolina.
-Yeah.

00:06:56.934 --> 00:06:58.400
And now he's become
this country star.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:01.300
So, Darius will be on
this weekend. Yeah.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.601
-Willie, I love you.
I love everything you do.

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:06.534
I love "Sunday Today."
I love "Morning Joe."

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:07.834
I love you on the "Today" show,

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:08.968
and I love you
on "The Tonight Show."

00:07:08.968 --> 00:07:10.434
-Thanks, man.
I'm so glad you're here.

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:11.901
-You're the best.
-Welcome back, guys.

00:07:11.901 --> 00:07:14.834
-Willie Geist. Check him out
on "Sunday Today"

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:17.300
and weekday mornings
on "Morning Joe."

